   "body": "Measuring the two paths exposed bugs that made the old latency numbers meaningless.\n\n- Consumer mapped shm `PROT_READ` but `pop()` writes `read_idx_` -> SIGSEGV on the first message. Now read-write, with a regression test.\n- Ticks stamped with the 1 ms cached clock -> +/-1 ms error. Now `precise_now_ns()` (CLOCK_MONOTONIC).\n- `high_resolution_clock` is `system_clock` on libstdc++ -> switched to `steady_clock`.\n- Subscriber slept after 1,000 idle polls -> busy-poll with pause/yield.\n- Clean build failed (missing `nlohmann_json` link, Catch2 v3 `Approx`).\n- Publisher hung if the consumer stopped.\n\nAdds `LatencyRecorder` (nearest-rank percentiles), CLI args, `scripts/bench.sh`, measured results in README.\n15 test cases / 114,866 assertions pass. Median: ~0.25 us shared memory vs ~20 us TCP+JSON.",
