   "body": "Closes #4\r\n\r\n## What this PR does\r\nAdds a `--verbose` flag to the `datalens clean` command that prints detailed information about the data cleaning pipeline operations. \r\n\r\n## Changes made\r\n* **`datalens/cleaning.py`**: Updated `clean_data()` to accept a `verbose` boolean. When `True`, the function computes and returns a dictionary of metrics alongside the cleaned DataFrame (tracking duplicates removed, rows/columns handled for missing values, and coerced dtypes). The default `verbose=False` behavior is unchanged so all existing tests remain green.\r\n* **`datalens/cli.py`**: Added the `@click.option` for `--verbose` to the `clean` command. If the user passes the flag, it unpacks the details dictionary and prints a formatted summary to the console.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria met\r\n- [x] `datalens clean data.csv --verbose` prints extra details (duplicates, missing values handled, coerced dtypes).\r\n- [x] Without `--verbose`, output is unchanged from current behavior.\r\n- [x] The underlying logic for computing details lives entirely in `datalens/cleaning.py` (not inline in the CLI), preserving testability.\r\n- [x] `pytest` passes locally.\r\n",
